            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="0921" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1821</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Russian
                        Affairs, Department of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Poole</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The attached text of telegraphic orders addressed to Admiral Bristol at
                    Constantinople by the Navy Department, January 12, 1922, has been furnished me
                    by Captain W. C. Cole, of the Navy Department.</p>
                <p>It is understood that these orders are transmitted to Admiral Bristol through
                    Admiral Niblack.</p>
                <p>The text of the orders is that agreed upon in conference between Captain Cole,
                    Mr. Herter, of the Department of Commerce, and myself</p>
                <closer><signed>D. C. P[<hi rendition="#small-caps">oole</hi>]</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d796-a1.xml" xpointer="d796-a1"/>
            </div>
